Description: live power status and quick actions for TLP
 A GTK4 panel showing what a laptop is doing with power right now: draw in
 watts, battery health and cycle count, and how long the battery will last at
 the current rate.
 .
 It also drives the settings people change most often — the TLP profile, the
 battery charge limit, Wi-Fi power saving, runtime power management for idle
 devices, and AMD adaptive backlight — through polkit, so the interface itself
 never runs as root.
 .
 Controls that the hardware cannot honour are detected and marked unsupported
 rather than silently doing nothing.
